<h2 class="bold" id="labelling-required-inputs"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="label#labelling-required-inputs">Labelling required inputs</a></h2>
<p>E-Commerce checkouts need to mark both required and optional fields explicitly. In other cases like a login or newsletter subscribtion it is not needed because of context, previous experience of the user and low number of fields.</p>
<p>Try to avoid optional fields in forms. But if you use them, you should at least clearly distinguish which input fields cannot be left blank by the user.</p>
<h3 class="bold" id="how-to-mark-required-fields"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="label#how-to-mark-required-fields">How to mark required fields</a></h3>
<p>If you need to mark field as a required, rather than mentioning &quot;required&quot; next to every header, use an asterisk with screenreader text.</p>
<h3 class="bold" id="how-to-mark-optional-fields"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="label#how-to-mark-optional-fields">How to mark optional fields</a></h3>
<p>Mark the optional fields in checkout or registration process with &quot;optional&quot; in words next to the label.</p>
