<h2 class="bold" id="links-and-buttons-in-labels"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="label#links-and-buttons-in-labels">Links and buttons in labels</a></h2>
<p>Don&#x27;t place interactive elements inside a label. Touchscreen devices often remove click listeners on label descendants, rendering them useless.</p>
<p>Interactive elements should be placed next to the label element, making sure that both label and action texts are provide meaningful information to screenreaders on their own. This is usually done with visually hiding portions of the instructions.</p>
